cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Measuring What You Cannot See: A Calibrated Study of Welfare and
  Equity Erosion in Proxy-Optimizing Incentive Allocation
message: "If you use this testbed or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "[Your given name]"
    family-names: "[Your family name]"
    affiliation: "[School / affiliation]"
abstract: >-
  An open, CPU-only agent-based testbed showing that a learning incentive
  allocator optimizing an observable retention proxy erodes unobserved
  employee satisfaction and cross-archetype equity, robustly across
  randomized worlds and under calibration to the IBM HR Analytics
  benchmark; and an honest negative result on satisfaction auditing as a
  remedy. Includes pre-registered falsification (kill-)tests. Simulation
  and analysis code were AI-assisted and disclosed.
keywords:
  - proxy optimization
  - Goodhart's law
  - incentive allocation
  - algorithmic fairness
  - negative results
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-07-24"
